  "raw_text": "67\n\nDiaura\n \n–\n \non what thing, in what thing, to what thing\n \n/ en qué cosa, a qué cosa\n\nDukia\n \n(\ndb,dbta,lrw,dict,dictu,bm,jl,fy,gf,ll,km\n;\n \nDukya\n-\nsln,bw,bh,lv,kt,sny\n;\n \nDukia\n,\nDukya\n-\nmy,dba\n)\n \n–\n \n(construct\nirregular of/de:\n \nDiara\n)\n \n–\n \nthe thing, the belonging, the article, the property, affair\n \n/ la cosa, la pertenencia, el\nartículo, la propiedad, el asunto\n\n(Construct other/otra:\n \nDuki\n \n–\n \nmy thing\n \n/ mi cosa;\n \nDukiam\n \n–\n \nyour thing\n \n/ tu cosa;\n \nAi dukia\n \n–\n \nhis/her/its/their thing\n \n/ su cosa)\n\nDukia daukaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nDukya daukaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto serve, to do the will of\n \n/ servir, hacer la voluntad de\n\nDukia dadaukra\n \n(a/t:\n \nDukya dadaukra\n-\nmy53\n) (n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nservant\n \n/ sirviente\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Aiseya 45:4\n):\n \nduki dadaukra Jekob\n \n–\n \nmy servant Jacob\n \n/ mi sirviente Jacob)\n\nTasba dukya nani\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nearth’s resources\n \n/ recursos de la tierra\n\nDiaura\n \n–\n \non what thing, in what thing, to what thing\n \n/ en qué cosa, a qué cosa\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu-07/20\n):\n \nYawan diaura lukaia sa, bara nahki tnata alkaia sip sa?\n \n–\n \nOn what thing are we to think (focus) upon, and how\nare we able to reach the end (goal)?\n \n/ ¿En qué debemos pensar (centrarnos) y cómo podemos alcanzar el fin (meta)?)\n\nDibil\n \n(\ndb,mwb,lfb,km,t33,bm\n;\n \nDebil\n-\ndba,dbta,lrw,sln,lv,sn,bh,my,rsg14\n)\n \n–\n \ndevil\n \n/ diablo\n\nSitan Dibil ba\n \n–\n \nSatan the Devil\n \n/\n \nSatanás el diablo\n\nDibors takaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nDiburs takaia\n-\nlv,bh,my\n)\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto become divorced\n \n/ divorciarse\n\nDibors takaia lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ndivorce\n \n/ divorcio\n\nDihbaia\n \n(v-transitive)\n \n–\n \nto pressure, to squeeze, to stock up, to pile up\n \n/ apretar, abastecer, amontonar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-1Sam 13:6\n):\n \nIsrael nanara ai dara walan witin nani ra karna pali dihbuya ba\n \n–\n \nIsrael now felt that they were putting great\npressure on them\n \n/ Israel ahora sentía que los estaba presionando mucho)\n\nDihbi prakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto stock up, to pile up, to press together\n \n/ abastecer, amontonar, presionar juntos\n\nDihwan\n \n–\n \nclose together, dense\n \n/ muy juntos, tupido\n\n(Note/Nota: This word could perhaps be viewed as being from\n \nDihwaia\n, which could be be an intransitive form of\n \nDihbaia\n.\nHowever,\n \nDihwaia\n \nis not in\n \ndict\n \nor\n \ndictu\n \nand other forms of it are not in\n \ndb\n. / Esta palabra tal vez podría verse como de\n \nDihwaia\n,\nque podría ser una forma intransitiva de\n \nDihbaia\n.\n \nSin embargo,\n \nDihwaia\n \nno está en\n \ndict\n \no\n \ndictu\n \ny otras formas de él no están en\n\ndb\n.\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nbîp nani ailal dihwan sa\n \n–\n \nmany cows close together\n \n/ muchas vacas muy juntas)\n\nDikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto erase, to remove, to rub off, to obliterate, to wipe, to scrub\n \n/ borrar, eliminar, quitar (frotando), limpiar,\nfregar\n\nDiki sakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto erase (writing), to remove, to wipe\n \n/ borrar (un escrito), eliminar\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\njl26\n):\n \npukpuka ba diki sakisa\n \n–\n \nremove\n \nthe\n \ndust\n \n/ quitar el polvo\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\ndb\n-\nAiseya\n \n25:8\n):\n \nDawan mita nakra laya nani sut diki sakbia\n \n–\n \nThe Lord will wipe away all tears\n \n/ El Señor\n \nsec\nará\n\ntodas las lágrimas\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nfg2\n):\n \nG\nâ\nd nina ba Baibil ailal wina diki sakan sa bara naha sirka ra, Dawan ulban sa …\n \n–\n \nGod's name is removed\n\nfrom many Bibles and in place of it, \"Lord\" is written …\n \n/ El nombre de Dios ha sido borrado de muchas Biblias y en su\n\nlugar, se escribe \"Señor\" …\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nJehova wan saurka nani diki sakisa\n \n–\n \nJehovah erases our sins\n \n/\n \nJehová borra nuestros pecados\n)\n\nDikia\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nany part of the body\n \n/ cualquier parte del cuerpo\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nDikiam klauhisa?\n \n–\n \nWhat part of your body aches?\n \n/ ¿Qué parte de tu cuerpo te duele?)\n\nDiksiunariu\n \n(\nlv\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \ndictionary\n \n/ diccionario\n\nDikwa\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncooking pot, cauldron, saucepan\n \n/ olla, porra, caldero, cacerola\n\n(Construct:\n \nDikwika\n-\ndict\n,\n \nDakawa\n-\ndb,dictu,dict\n)\n\nDildil\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nbutterfly\n \n/ mariposa\n\nDimaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto go in, to enter, to get in, to attend, to get dressed, to put on clothing, to dress, to arrive\n \n/ entrar, vestirse,\nasistir, ponerse ropa, llegar\n\n(Note\n/Nota\n: used to describe the\n \nsun setting\n \n/ s\ne usa para\n \ndescribir la puesta de sol\n \n(\nmy49\n-\nDimuya\n))\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-07/19\n):\n \nMan kangrigisan ra dimram taim, rayakam ra chens ailal daukram?\n \n–\n \nWhen you entered into the congregation\n(came into the truth), did you make many changes in your life?\n \n/ Cuando ingresaste a la congregación (entraste en la verdad),\n¿hiciste muchos cambios en tu vida?)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nhf-17\n):\n \nMan nani ba laki kaikaia sma dîa pitka kat want sma aisikam nani ba maritkam lâka bisniska ra dimbia\n \n–\n \nYou have\nto examine up to what point you want your parents to get into the business (personal matters) of your marriage\n \n/ Tienes que\nexaminar hasta qué punto quieres que tus padres entren en el negocio (asuntos personales) de tu matrimonio)\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nmwb\n-\n01/22\n):\n \nBaibil stadi tatakra nani ba aidrubanka nani ra ban dimisa taim, spirit lainka ra kau isti p\nâ\nwisa.\n \n–\n \nWhen the\n\nBible student attends meetings regularly, they grow spiritually more quickly.\n \n/ Cuando el estudiante de la Biblia asiste a las\n\nreuniones regularmente, crece espiritualmente más\n \nrápidamente.)",
